[resource]
script = ExtResource("1_emqki")
dialogue_id = "mq_2_10_begin"
record_title = "Era 二: Places of Power"
text = "PAGE: scribe(SHRINE_PRIMARY), teo(SHRINE_SECONDARY)
scribe: Oh Enlightened One, I prayed, and you were silent.
scribe: You promised to walk among us, yet we are still alone.
scribe: But I understand now.
scribe: You have already given us everything we needed in the sacred glyphs.
scribe: You were telling us to use your power to prepare, not just wait.
scribe: Well, use it we will!
scribe: Forgive me.
scribe: No more will I merely pray.
scribe: From this day on, I will act.

PAGE: scribe(PORTAL_NETWORK), monk(GENERIC), AUDIENCE
scribe: Listen well!
scribe: The glyphs were instructions.
scribe: We, fools, mistook them for promises, but they are tools.
scribe: Tools we will use to focus the Enlightened One's power emanating through the great statue.
scribe: Each stroke touches a part of the world.
scribe: It was all in the old scrolls.
scribe: Air, earth, fire, [i]everything[/i] will obey our commands if we direct the energies right.
monk: The Enlightened One's energies?
scribe: No, no, the energies of the world!
scribe: They saturate the shards themselves, flowing with the rivers and knotting in old trees.
scribe: When we tap into them with the right glyphs, they come to life.
scribe: That is what makes our actions auspicious!
monk: But how do we know the rules?
scribe: The teachings give us the tools, but we must experiment if we are to wield them.
scribe: We will find the veins where the world's pulse is strongest, and we will strike.

PAGE: historian(STUDIO_SECONDARY), scribe(STUDIO_PRIMARY)
historian: You preach as if you're sure, but what do we really know about these powers?
historian: What if they aren't so harmless?
scribe: We have no time to wait.
scribe: Every day the shards spread farther apart.
scribe: Inaction has failed us once, and I won't let it happen again!
historian: In that case I will write down what we find.
historian: If your plan fails, we'll need those lessons.
scribe: Very well!
scribe: Stay in your archive.
scribe: When you are ready to record the laws of the world, I will have carved them into the earth.
historian: At least our foolishness will be well documented..."
metadata/_custom_type_script = "uid://jtkfcsyiryo4"
